{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"A polynomial replacement is slightly slower in its conservative form, but it has two removable FMAs. I’m tightening it to minimax degree-5/degree-4 approximations (worst real-valued errors ≈6.8e-5 for sine and 6.0e-4 for cosine), then I’ll keep it only if direct timing beats the native instructions."}}
