{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining geometry gain is only noise-level (two-row/wave groups are a few tenths of a microsecond better on the largest shape). Before committing that, I’m checking whether CDNA’s native trig instruction already performs periodic reduction outside its documented principal interval; if so, one multiply/floor/subtract sequence can disappear. This is being tested numerically first."}}
